CC0 1.0 Universal

The person who associated a work with this deed has dedicated the work to the
public domain by waiving all of his or her rights to the work worldwide under
copyright law, including all related and neighboring rights, to the extent
allowed by law.

You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial
purposes, all without asking permission.


COPYRIGHT AND RELATED RIGHTS WAIVER

I.     Copyright and Related Rights.

Copyright and related rights include, but are not limited to, the following
rights: copyright, including rights related to the distribution, public
reproduction, public display, public performance, communication to the public
as well as translation, adaptation, arrangement, and other derivative works,
related rights such as performance, broadcasting, and moral rights, in all
cases to the extent allowed by law.

II.    Waiver.

To the greatest extent permitted by, but not in contravention of, applicable
law, the person who has associated work with this deed (the "Affirmer")
voluntarily and permanently relinquishes, waives, and surrenders all of the
Affirmer's copyright and related rights in the work worldwide under copyright
law, including all related and neighboring rights, to the extent allowed by
law.

The Affirmer makes this dedication for the benefit of each member of the
public at large and to the detriment of the Affirmer's heirs and
successors.  The Affirmer intends this dedication to be an overt act of
relinquishment in perpetuity of all present and future rights in the work to
the greatest extent permitted by law.

If the Affirmer's jurisdiction does not permit the relinquishment of
copyright and related rights to the extent provided above, the Affirmer
hereby grants to any and all persons on a royalty-free, non-exclusive,
perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide license to exercise any and all copyright
and related rights in the work for any purpose whatsoever, without any
conditions, unless such conditions are required by law.

III.   Limitations and Disclaimers.

The Affirmer makes the dedication and waiver for the benefit of the public as
a whole and reaffirms that this dedication and waiver are made voluntarily.

The Affirmer makes no representations concerning the work, including
without limitation, representations about the work's source, originality,
accuracy, or fitness for any purpose.  The affirmer disclaims all liability
and responsibility with respect to the work to the fullest extent permitted
by law.

